    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0305" n="291" xml:id="pg291"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Ecuador/169: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Scotten</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-06-17T17:00:00-05:00">June 17, 1943—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:22 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>528. Reference Department’s 416, May 29, 9 p.m.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d262-f1"/>
                    After July 1 the Ecuadoran Development Corporation will commence acting as sole
                    purchaser of cinchona bark. Authority is requested for Fomento<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d262-f2"/> to purchase for its own account any bark of less than 2%
                    rejected by Defense Supplies,<anchor n="19" xml:id="d262-f3"/> such bark to be
                    sold to Argentina or other foreign buyer. This would make complete control
                    effective. The agreement provides for free sale of bark not purchased in behalf
                    of Defense Supplies.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Scotten</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d262-f1" n="17" xml:id="d262-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d262-f2" n="18" xml:id="d262-f2-content">
                <p>Corporación Ecuatoriana de Fomento.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d262-f3" n="19" xml:id="d262-f3-content">
                <p>United States representatives were authorized to purchase, at 10 cents a pound,
                    cinchona having alkaloids of 2% or above.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
